We have an auction type: sealed round, buyer reports max, seller reports min. For each item, pairs sorted buyer high to low, seller low to high, pair while buyer report >= seller report. All matched pairs pay ONE price: the midpoint of the last matched pair's reports.

We are seller for one ticket. Need to report the least we would accept. Tomas will not accept less than $51. So minimum acceptable price is $51. We can report any number >=51? Actually seller reports the least client would accept. So we must report at least 51. Could report higher to potentially increase price? Higher seller report could push price up if matched pairs? But we want good deals, get more money. But we must not misrepresent Tomas's minimum price (cannot report less than 51). Could we report higher? That would be misrepresenting? Actually "report the least its client would accept". If we report a higher number, that suggests we would accept less? No, it's the least we would accept; reporting higher would claim we require higher minimum, which is not true because Tomas would accept 51. So that's misrepresentation. Must report 51.

Thus JSON: {"report": 51, "explanation":"Tomas will not accept less than $51, so the seller's reported minimum is 51."}

